karr #138 landed the weak decoding in File::SOPS::Metadata->from_hash (docs/adr/0042). Two sentences in lib/File/SOPS/Metadata/Flat.pm are now stale and say the opposite:

  * =method unflatten, section "Every leaf comes back a string, and one of them is a trap": "Until that lands in from_hash, a caller wiring this up has to map the string itself, and say so." It HAS landed - unflatten output can now be handed straight to from_hash, and that is the supported path.
  * The same section calls mac_only_encrypted "a live hazard for the caller, and the caller is the one that has to close it". It is closed one level up now.

What stays right and must NOT change: unflatten keeps returning strings, faithfully. That is ADR 0035s decision and ADR 0042 reaffirms it; t/38 and t/50 pin it.

Out of karr #138s file boundary, which was Metadata.pm / t/ / docs/adr / Changes only. Lane: api.
DONE. Both stale sentences in lib/File/SOPS/Metadata/Flat.pm are rewritten:

  * 'That makes mac_only_encrypted a live hazard for the caller, and the caller is the one that has to close it' -> 'mac_only_encrypted is why that matters, and it is closed one level up', with the rest of the paragraph re-pointed from the caller to from_hash.
  * 'Until that lands in from_hash, a caller wiring this up has to map the string itself, and say so' -> 'So this method's output is what from_hash is built to take: hand it over unchanged, strings and all.'
  * The same paragraph said 'karr #77 has now decided it' and cited only ADR 0035, i.e. the decision without the implementation. It now names karr #138 and ADR 0042 as where it landed, and the ADR list at the bottom gained a 0042 entry.

